Draft date: November 2026

[[Written for Drafter for Claude's tests only (packages/mcp/test). Every line is original. It is not an in-app sample.]]

# Act One

INT. JUNE'S KITCHEN - MORNING

= A year on. June keeps the log every morning, whether or not the radio speaks.
[[Color: blue]]

The same kitchen, a new calendar. JUNE (72) writes the date at the top of a ledger, then the time, then the word "nothing", neatly.

JUNE
(writing)
Nothing. Again.

The kettle starts. The radio doesn't.

EXT. FEED STORE - DAY

= Dell, the deputy, asks June about the ledger.
[[Color: yellow]]

A loading dock, sacks of feed on a pallet. June signs for an order. DELL (20s), deputy, holds the door for her and doesn't let go of it.

DELL
People say you write down the radio.

JUNE
People say a lot of things on a loading dock.

DELL
Do you?

JUNE
I write down what I hear. Mostly I hear the kettle.

INT. AMARA'S VAN - NIGHT

= Amara is back, with a year of recordings and one that doesn't fit.
[[Color: green]]

The van, tidier now. Amara plays a clip for Eli, older by a year and taller by a head.

AMARA
Every broadcast since last autumn is a repeat. Same words, same order.

ELI
Except?

AMARA
Except this one.

She taps a key. A man's voice, slow, reading out a list of names.

# Act Two

INT. RAY'S WORKSHOP - DAY

= Ray knows one of the names on the list.
[[Color: blue]]

Ray listens with his eyes closed. Amara holds the laptop on her knees.

RAY
Stop it there.

She stops it.

RAY (CONT'D)
Go back two.

She does.

RAY (CONT'D)
That's my brother. He's been dead since before you were born.

EXT. SIGNAL HILL - DUSK

= The four of them climb the hill to wait for the list to finish.
[[Color: green]]

June with the ledger under her arm. Eli with the coil. Ray with a folding chair. Amara last, carrying nothing, watching the sky.

ELI
What if it reads one of us?

JUNE
Then I'll write it down, and we'll argue with it.

INT. JUNE'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

= The list ends with a name nobody knows.
[[Color: blue]]

They are back at the table. The ledger open. The radio on.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
And finally, the keeper of the log.

Everyone looks at June. June looks at the page, at her own handwriting.

JUNE
That's the first true thing it's said all year.

FADE OUT.
